{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtii"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE11neidhardtIIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","role":"symbol","title":"neidhardtII","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, B♭→F, F→C — are each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, E♭→B♭ — are pure. The circle closes exactly:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"From "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Neidhardt relabeled this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specification “Large City” in his 1732 revision."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt II (“Small City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtII":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII","title":"neidhardtII","role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtii","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt II (“Small City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}]},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","title":"IvorTuning","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"role":"symbol","title":"WellTemperament","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}